    "description": "Tested software for the V22 Osprey, M346, C17, and E2C aircraft and Non-Vital Station Computer train software using the VAX, ALPHA, Sun, and Tornado, Archimedes, and Visual C++ 6.0.\nCreated and reviewed Operational Concept Documents, Software Requirements Specification, Interface Requirements, and Software Design Documents using Microsoft Word and Excel.\nCoded software for:\nBST ProMark's G5 and Genius: Camera systems which are used to inspect the results of industrial printing presses using Visual C++ 6.0.\nMetro North Railroad's Genesis II and M7, and PATH PA5 passenger and freight train simulators used to train engineers, including the braking and propulsion systems, malfunctions, and evaluation using Visual Basic 6.0 and Visual FORTRAN 5.0.  \nAssisted in the creation and maintenance of the simulator database using Microsoft Access.\nCreated Three Dimensional models using 3D World Studio, AC3D, and various texture makers for use in NY-NJ Port Authority Trans-Hudson Train Simulator.\nConducted nightly backups.",
